        "notes": [
            "In a careful hand: \"If you find this, tell my mother in the river town that I am well, and that I am not coming home.\"",
            "Scratched in charcoal: \"Owed to Hob the miller, three pence. Paid. Paid! PAID.\"",
            "A child's drawing of a fish with legs, and a name you cannot read.",
            "\"To whoever finds this: the eels in this river are the size of a man's arm. Do not swim at the bend.\"",
            "A love-letter, smudged past reading but for the last line: \"...at the willow, when the bells ring.\"",
            "A list: \"Salt. Nails. A new rope for the well. Do NOT buy from the tinker again.\"",
            "\"I threw this in at the source. How far did it get? Write the place here:\" Below, three names of towns in three different inks.",
            "A prayer to the river, asking it to carry away a fever. Whoever wrote it hoped hard."
        ]
    },
    "nets": {
        "_doc": "Fishing nets the player sets in a river (across it), a pond, a lake or the sea (systems/riverNets.js; on the street map ui/innerMapRiverDrift.js). One net to a hex, maxNets in all. A river net catches what drifts down into it (cap things in all, then the rest slips by); every net takes fish day by day: fishRolls tries a day, each fishChance x seasonMult, from the fish table of its water. A river net also snags a stray find now and then (snagChance a day). Fish left in a net longer than fishKeepDays are lost (eels, crabs, rot). Each day a net may tear (tearChance x (1 + days set / ageDays), x stormMult in a storm; a torn net catches nothing until mended with mendCost) or be stolen while you are away (theftChance; townTheft near a town). stillReach: cells from a pond net within which a thing thrown in is gathered up. reach: how near (cells) you must stand to set, haul or take up a net. catchUpDays: days caught up at most when time passes at a stroke. stakeBite: the extra chance of a bite casting a line from beside your own set net (the fish gather at it).",
